    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a challenging slate today, highlighted by a premier matchup for **Junior Caminero** (72.81), who stands as our strongest play. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a high-upside spot in the two-hole against a hittable opponent, with his 11% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s projected skill providing the necessary ceiling to lead the lineup. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (65.71) earns a high recommendation despite hitting eighth; his 14% dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed starter outweighs his lower spot in the order, offering the best speed-based upside we have available today to hunt those critical stolen bases. **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) rounds out the top tier, capitalizing on a favorable park factor and a significant boost from the matchup against Severino.\n\nOur toughest decision on the bench was leaving **Hyeseong Kim** (48.21) out of the starting nine. While **Hyeseong Kim** remains a viable depth piece, his profile was ultimately squeezed out by the more favorable platoon splits assigned to **Dillon Dingler** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. We are also closely monitoring the risks inherent in our high-profile starts: **Yordan Alvarez** (57.58) and **Trea Turner** (58.04) are both facing elite-tier arms in deGrom and Chandler, respectively. The negative SP skill adjustments for these sluggers underscore the volatility of today\u2019s slate. While **Luke Raley** (57.19) and **Kyle Schwarber** (56.56) remain in the active lineup, they must navigate the pressure of these high-xERA matchups without the luxury of premium park or platoon safety nets. Managers should keep a close watch on **Carson Benge** (52.31), as his L/L matchup risk remains a potential drag on his efficiency if the opposing starter finds an early groove.",
